(area "prose" :when "the turn may be about to end, or a note says part of the last reply was skipped or run as code")

(memory "prose/skipped" :when "a note says part of the last reply was skipped, ignored or run as code, or the user asks why")
Skipped forms and asides:
- Prose reads come back as "skipped … note" with the next user message, not at the time. No apology, no explaining the skip, no restating the previous answer. User asked something new: answer only that.
- A note alone arrives with the next user message. Act silently: do not repeat that shape.
- Outside the agent loop, a form-less program is a no-op. REPL and driver behaviour, not core language.

(memory "prose/final" :when "the task looks done and the agent is about to end the turn, or work keeps running toward the step cap")
- Prose around a form is ignored. Prose with no form is the final answer to user, e.g. "the sum is 3".
